## Principles
- Use existing components first. Use npx shadcn@latest search to check registries before writing custom UI. Check community registries too.
- Compose, don't reinvent. Settings page = Tabs + Card + form controls. Dashboard = Sidebar + Card + Chart + Table.
- Use built-in variants before custom styles: `variant={ButtonVariant.Outline}`, `size={ButtonSize.Small}`, etc.
- Use semantic colors. bg-primary, text-muted-foreground — never raw values like bg-blue-500.

# shadcn/ui bases

- The `style` in `components.json` is the app's only style. Add every primitive with `shadcn add` (CLI or MCP) against that config. Never paste a component from another style, another registry, a blog post, or the HTML prototype.
- The CLI output is the source of truth. Re-homing into `shared/ui/<name>/` moves code; it does not rewrite it:
  - Keep every exported part, prop, `data-slot` attribute, and Radix import exactly as generated (`radix-ui` or `@radix-ui/react-*` — whichever the CLI wrote).
  - Move class strings into `styles.ts` verbatim and in the same order, including every `data-[state=*]:`, `animate-in`, `animate-out`, `fade-*`, `zoom-*`, `slide-in-from-*`, and `duration-*` class.
  - Allowed edits only: deleting the registry's comments, kebab-case file names, props types to `types.ts`, closed-set constants in `constants.ts`, user-facing literals (the `sr-only` "Close") to `t(commonKeys…)`, `FormMessage` passing the error through `translateMessage`, and `Button`'s default `type`.
- Global CSS imports the animation stylesheet the CLI configured (`@import "tw-animate-css"` on Tailwind v4) exactly once. No extra `@keyframes`, `--animate-*` tokens, or a second animation library.
- Motion utilities exist only in these bases. Feature, entity, widget, and page code never adds `animate-*`, `transition-*`, `duration-*`, `fade-*`, `slide-*`, or `zoom-*` to a primitive — it overrides the base's `data-state` animation.
- A caller composes parts in the order of the registry demo (`get_item_examples_from_registries`, e.g. `dialog-demo`): `DialogContent` → `DialogHeader` (`DialogTitle`, `DialogDescription`) → body → `DialogFooter` (`DialogClose asChild`).
- A new look is a new `cva` variant in the base's `styles.ts`, added by the shared-UI step — never a call-site `className` override of color, radius, border, shadow, padding, or typography.
- Each closed-set prop gets a constant object in `constants.ts`, derived from the `cva` table: `ButtonVariant`, `ButtonSize`, `BadgeVariant`, `AlertVariant`; `Input` exports `InputType`. `Button` also exports `ButtonType` and defaults `type` to `ButtonType.Button`, so callers omit it except for `ButtonType.Submit`.

Procedure: `shadcn-usage` skill.
